    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-24T00:32:51Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Inca engineers built terraces that slowed erosion and created level growing ground on steep slopes; their stonework also helped manage water across varied mountain climates.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#5d62b3c7fb94691b8e6c62fecce038a5a5a517e1b4d9a7dd974a48f205525772</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-24T00:32:51Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">South Korea’s kimjang tradition brings neighbours together to make and share kimchi for winter; fermentation preserves vegetables, turning seasonal abundance into food that lasts.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#31d9b2c8183aad7487f6cd914cf880bec7e980e8e7fd59e1486d874aed171175</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-24T00:32:51Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">For two minutes, watch a patch of ground or a tree from where you are; notice one wild creature, or signs such as tracks, chewed leaves or a spider’s web.</div>
    </content>
